## Why Wave 57-Hodge exists

Wave 56-Hodge encoded the Fermat quintic CY3 substrate
`X₅ = {Σ x_i^5 = 0 ⊂ ℙ⁴}` with the named open Prop
`hodge_codim2_quintic_CY3_voisin_known_case_subprop` left as a
single load-bearing hypothesis. The Wave 56 file's substrate-level
encoding is *definitional*; the **geometric** content (does every
integral `(2,2)`-Hodge class on the actual `X₅` admit a curve
representative?) was deferred as OPEN.

This file gives the *first concrete attack* on that geometric
content by splitting it into **two sub-cases**:

  * **(a) Dwork pencil sub-case** — the one-parameter Dwork family
    `X_λ = {Σ x_i^5 + λ · x_0 x_1 x_2 x_3 x_4 = 0 ⊂ ℙ⁴}`. For this
