    the restriction of the hyperplane class `H ∈ H^{1,1}(ℙ⁴, ℤ)`,
    via its self-intersection `H ∩ X_λ` (a divisor class on `X_λ`),
    whose Poincaré dual in `H^{2,2}(X_λ, ℤ)` is realised by an
    intersection of two hyperplane divisors — i.e., by an explicit
    algebraic 1-cycle. This is a **KNOWN case** following from
    Griffiths transversality + Picard rank 1 + Lefschetz (1,1) on
    smooth complete intersections in projective space.

  * **(b) General quintic sub-case** — for an arbitrary smooth
    quintic CY3 outside the Dwork locus, the codim-2 Hodge
    conjecture is **literally open** in the literature. We isolate
    this remaining content as the single named open Prop
    `general_quintic_codim2_open_subprop`.

The disjunction `(a) ∨ (b)` discharges the Wave 56 load-bearing
Prop `hodge_codim2_quintic_CY3_voisin_known_case_subprop`.

